---
const links = [
  ["Conjunction + clause", "We waited because the bridge was closed.", "The words after because have a subject and a verb."],
  ["Preposition + noun phrase", "We waited after lunch.", "Lunch is a noun. There is no new clause."],
  ["Adverb", "Later, we crossed the bridge.", "Later places the action in time."]
];
---

<div class="topic-sheet">
  <h1>Sentence Structure - Words in a sentence</h1>
  <p>
    A word’s job is decided in its sentence. The parts-of-speech sheets name each job. Here, use them to see
    how a sentence is built.
  </p>
  <section class="summary-block summary-sand">
    <h2>After lunch, those curious children quietly explored the cave because it was cool.</h2>
    <p><strong>After</strong> preposition + <strong>lunch</strong> noun.</p>
    <p><strong>Those</strong> determiner, <strong>curious</strong> adjective, <strong>children</strong> noun.</p>
    <p><strong>Quietly</strong> adverb, <strong>explored</strong> verb, <strong>the</strong> determiner, <strong>cave</strong> noun.</p>
    <p><strong>Because</strong> conjunction, <strong>it</strong> pronoun, <strong>was</strong> verb, <strong>cool</strong> adjective.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="summary-block summary-blue">
    <h2>Time, place and cause</h2>
    <table class="punct-table summary-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="th-feature" scope="col">Form</th>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">Example</th>
          <th class="th-rule" scope="col">Clue</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          links.map(([form, example, clue]) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{form}</th>
              <td>{example}</td>
              <td>{clue}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
  <div class="trap-card trap-compact">
    <section class="trap">
      <h2>The same word can change class</h2>
      <p>We left <strong>after lunch</strong>: preposition. We left <strong>after the rain stopped</strong>: conjunction.</p>
      <p><strong>Light</strong> is a noun in “the light shone” and an adjective in “a light bag.”</p>
      <p><strong>This</strong> is broken: pronoun. <strong>This lantern</strong> is broken: determiner.</p>
      <p>Not every adverb ends in -ly (<em>soon, here, often</em>), and <em>friendly</em> can be an adjective.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
